--- Source code analysis ---

File: plugins/huaweicloud-core/src/safety-policy.mjs (lines 104-110)
Function: applyCommandRiskRules(base, normalizedArgs, options)
  if (base.decision === 'deny' || options.skipRiskRules === true) {
    return base;  // Early return if already denied
  }
  const risk = evaluateCommandRisk(commandRiskText(normalizedArgs, options));
  return mergeRiskDecision(base, risk);

File: plugins/huaweicloud-core/src/risk-rule-engine.mjs (lines 123-139)
Function: mergeRiskDecision(base, risk)
  if (risk.decision === 'deny') {
    return {
      ...base,
      decision: 'deny',  // OVERRIDES any 'allow' from allowWrites
      risk: topFinding.category,
      reason: topFinding.message,
      blockedByRiskRule: true,
      findings: risk.findings,
    };
  }

ANALYSIS: The risk rule engine runs AFTER the allowWrites check. If a deny-severity
rule matches, mergeRiskDecision overrides the decision to 'deny' regardless of
the base decision from allowWrites. This ensures preflight safety checks always run.

